==Trivia==
*Way Big is one of [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken's]] favorite aliens.<ref>''[[Ken 10]]''</ref>
*Way Big could be eaten by a [[Gourmand]] if he were chopped up into bite-sized chunks.{{Refn|[[:File:Upchuck May Eat a To'kustar.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Way Big could be subdued by the Hephestan Neuro Grip, but only if this move were to be performed by beings with hands much bigger than [[Slapstrike|Slapstrike's]].{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Hephestan Neuro Grip.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Slapstrike Cannot Use Hephestan Neuro Grip on Way Big.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Way Big and [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]] are the only aliens who have ever defeated [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].
*Way Big is one of four aliens to make their debut in a movie or special; the others being [[Eon (Transformation)|Eon]], [[Nanomech]], and [[Shocksquatch]].
*Way Big is one of three aliens to have been unlocked by [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]]; the others being [[Bullfrag]] and [[Atomix]].
*Way Big is one of the only five aliens who escaped from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]; the others are [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]], [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]], Ghostfreak, and [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]].
*Way Big is one of four regular aliens to be temporarily destroyed and removed from the original Omnitrix/[[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]], the others being Chromastone, [[Feedback]], and [[Swampfire]].
*Way Big is one of only five aliens who appeared in each series of the Classic Continuity; the other four are Upchuck, [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]], Diamondhead, and [[Ghostfreak]].
**So far, Diamondhead, Cannonbolt, and Way Big are the only aliens to have appeared in every series in the [[Ben 10 (Franchise)|franchise]], including the Reboot.
*Evil Way Big's design is identical to [[Albedo]]'s [[Evil Way Big]] from ''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Cosmic Destruction|Cosmic Destruction]]'', except with a different chest badge.
*Way Big's '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''' design was made by [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]].{{Refn|[[:File:Tom Designed S3 & S4 Characters.png]]|group = TNP}} The first prototype design he made was approved as the crew was very busy at the time.{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big and Ditto No Prototypes.PNG]]|group = TNP}}
**Way Big's '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]'''/'''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' design was created by [[Glenn Wong]], with color styling by Chris Hooten.{{Refn|https://archive.ph/zzjTO|group = GW}}
**Way Big's '''Omniverse''' design was made by Derrick alongside either [[Steven Choi]] or [[Chap Yaep]].{{Refn|[[:File:OV Way Big Designers.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Some of the Aliens Designed by Derrick in OV.png]]|group = DJW}} It would later serve as the basis for [[Way Big (Reboot)|Way Big's]] design in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|reboot]].
*Way Big was originally envisioned in the script of '''''[[Ben 10: Secret of the Omnitrix|Secret of the Omnitrix]]''''' and designed accordingly as an alien that could grow to giant size,{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Size Changing 2.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big's Cosmic Powers.PNG]]|group = TNP|name=cosmic1}} with his height meant to be variable,{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Size Changing.png]]|group = TNP|name=cosmic2}}{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Size Changer.png]]|group = TNP}} though [[Thomas N. Perkins IV]] could not recall what the final decision on the height was.{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Size Alteration.png]]|group = TNP|name = size}}{{Refn|group = TNP|[[:File:Way Big Size Changing 3.png]]}}
**[[Duncan Rouleau]] believes that Way Big does indeed have such an ability,{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Can Change Size.png]]|group = DR}} though [[Charlotte McDuffie]] disagrees, stating that [[Dwayne McDuffie]] and [[Glen Murakami]] wanted Way Big to stay big.{{Refn|group = CM|[[:File:Charlotte on Way Big size changing.png]]}}
**At that point, Way Big did not have any other powers, such as his cosmic beams, or any backstory. The other powers and abilities were added by future writers.{{Refn|group = TNP|name=cosmic1}}{{Refn|group = TNP|name=cosmic2}}
**Similarly, Way Big's frill was also not meant to be a weak point.{{Refn|group = TNP|[[:File:TNP unaware of weak fin.png]]}} Thomas N. Perkins IV was not a fan of the fin being a weakness,{{Refn|group = TNP|name=cosmic2}} commenting that it would not make sense for such a prominent feature to be one,{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Weak Fin.png]]|group = TNP}} and called it an "unfortunate choice".{{Refn|[[:File:Thomas Perkins' Opinion on Way Big's Weak Frill.png]]|group = TNP}}
*[[Charlotte McDuffie]] once incorrectly claimed that Way Big was created by [[Dwayne McDuffie]] and [[Glen Murakami]],{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne & Glen created Way Big.png]]|group = CM}} while [[Joe Kelly]] could not recall.{{Refn|[[:File:Dwayne & Glen created Way Big 2.png]]|group =JK}} She later admitted that she didn't know about the creation of Way Big.{{Refn|[[:File:Charlotte doesn't know Way Big's creation.png]]|group = CM}}
**Thomas N. Perkins IV and Duncan Rouleau credited the entire "team" at the time for the creation of Way Big, not a singular entity.{{Refn|[[:File:OS Crew Created Way Big.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|[[:File:OS Crew Created Way Big 2.png]]|group = DR}}
*A [[Way Big's Predator|predator]] for Way Big was conceptualized during the production of '''Omniverse''',{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big Predator Concept.png]]|group = DJW}} however, art for it was never drawn and it ultimately went unimplemented. Derrick J. Wyatt imagined the alien as a cross between a sentient virus and an infestation of mites and fleas.{{Refn|https://archive.fo/VeEQx|group = DJW}}
*Way Big's design and fighting style are based on the heroes of the '''[[w:c:ultra:Ultraman (series)|Ultraman]]''' series.
**For example, Way Big's cosmic ray attack is similar to Ultraman's signature technique, the [[w:c:ultra:Ultra Beam|Specium Ray]].
**Both Way Big and Ultraman had [[w:c:ultra:Color Timer|time limit settings]] (the former due to limits on transformation durations of the [[Omnitrix]])
**In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Way Big speaks with a [[Wikipedia:Japan|Japanese]] accent, further equating him to Ultraman.
**However, Way Big's vulnerable to electricity makes him different from Ultraman, who is immune to it.
**Thomas N. Perkins IV claims that he did not intentionally design Way Big as an Ultraman-inspired alien, but noted that Ultraman was a formative part of his childhood, so some elements of Ultraman's design made it into Way Big's.{{Refn|[[:File:Thomas Perkins Channeled Some of Ultraman Into Way Big.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|[[:File:Thomas Perkins Did Not Intentionally Design Way Big As Ultraman-Inspired.png]]|group = TNP}}
*Way Big is [[Joe Kelly]]'s favorite alien.{{Refn|group = JK|https://twitter.com/yasinemiralkaya/status/1771639134660055254}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] viewed Way Big as Ben's sixth most powerful alien.{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DJW}} Prior to [[Atomix]]'s introduction, [[Matt Wayne]] guessed that Way Big was a runner-up to [[Alien X (Classic)|Alien X]] in terms of power.{{Refn|[[:File:Way Big vs Toepick MW.png]]|group = MW|name = powerful}}

